2026-05-13 23:07:31,538 subagents.b_hld_v_agent.agent INFO hld_v[important] externalContracts[13].responseShape — "cart_token": "text" — the LLD-leak checklist explicitly identifies `_token` as an integration-specific ID suffix (rule 1). The LLD will generate a field named after Shopify's internal cart identifier convention rather than a domain-neutral term, making the contract integration-coupled.
2026-05-13 23:07:31,538 subagents.b_hld_v_agent.agent INFO hld_v[important] triggers[1] — "a product variant's availability changes — either its stock reaches zero or the product is permanently deleted" conflates two structurally distinct external signals into one trigger. Inventory-level changes and product/variant deletion events originate from different platform topics with different payloads and different signalFields (inventory level versus deletion confirmation). The LLD cannot resolve which webhook mapping to generate, and a single handler written for one payload shape will misread the other.
2026-05-13 23:07:31,538 subagents.b_hld_v_agent.agent INFO hld_v[important] capabilities[12] — "fetch-live-variant-availability" sets `integration: "shopify-admin"` but is consumed in the customer-facing widget request path (the widget calls it before the customer adds to cart). The Admin API requires merchant-scoped credentials that must never be reachable from a customer session; routing a storefront request through an Admin API call exposes those credentials to a customer-facing attack surface. The LLD will build this integration path as specified and produce an insecure architecture.
2026-05-13 23:07:31,538 subagents.b_hld_v_agent.agent INFO hld_v[minor] capabilities[19] — "evaluate-bundle-health" is declared `kind: "compute"` but its description ends with "then apply the resulting health status change" — implying a write. The spec defines compute as pure logic over data already in hand; any application of a result is a write and belongs to a separate write capability. This description will mislead the LLD into blending the compute and write phases inside one handler.
